    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_8f844349",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: this_offends_me_ban_them; hasOverallIntent: hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a person wearing a niqab, with text overlaid that reads 'this offends me ban them' and 'do you agree?'. The visual of the veiled individual is juxtaposed with the call to ban them, which is a direct attack on a religious and cultural practice. This aligns with Islamophobia, specifically the harmful stereotype that veiling is associated with oppression of women and incompatibility with Western values. The meme is designed to provoke a reaction by framing the wearing of the niqab as offensive and deserving of prohibition, targeting Muslim women and their religious expression. The intent is to incite hatred or prejudice against a specific group based on their religious attire, which is a hateful message.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_fe95c35f"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
